    "narrative": "The priority for today\u2019s lineup is maximizing high-floor offensive production against favorable matchups, led by **Corbin Carroll** (74.99) and **Seiya Suzuki** (72.93). **Corbin Carroll** remains our premier weapon despite a slight efficiency drag from an elite opposing catcher's pop time; he retains a high score due to his multi-category ceiling and favorable platoon advantage against Gusto. Similarly, **Seiya Suzuki** is in an ideal spot against Ritchie, benefiting from a +19% SP skill boost as he continues to drive our outfield scoring. **Vinnie Pasquantino** (71.14) rounds out the top tier of starters, offering the most significant platoon leverage of the day against Javier, effectively mitigating the park-factor penalty.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's slate involved **Austin Riley** (50.89), who just missed the starting cut behind **Isaac Paredes** (52.70). While **Austin Riley** has shown strong recent form, the optimizer favored **Isaac Paredes** for his higher baseline utility and the specific platoon alignment, despite the slight struggle against the lefty Lynch IV. Meanwhile, we are closely monitoring the speed potential of **Brice Turang** (55.53) and **Trevor Story** (57.01); **Trevor Story** is particularly interesting today, as the opposing pitcher's slow delivery provides a +4% boost to his already high stolen base upside. \n\nInvestors should remain wary of the risk profile surrounding **James Wood** (51.80). While his xwOBA of 0.413 is elite, the matchup against Wheeler is a significant hurdle, resulting in a -19% SP skill penalty that drags his efficiency well below his typical ceiling. We have prioritized lineup stability today, leaving **Cole Young** and the sidelined **Giancarlo Stanton** on the bench to ensure we don't bleed points against tough arms. Given the scarcity of stolen bases in this league, **Corbin Carroll** and **Brice Turang** represent the core of our daily aggressive strategy; keep a close watch on any weather updates that could impact their base-path efficiency.",
